{
  "summary": "P1 \u2013 office-wide internet outage. Reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3, America/New_York): \"The whole office just lost internet. Nobody on the floor can work.\" Triage: P1, network_vpn, all users on the floor blocked. Checked: account active, no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online=true, last check-in 2026-10-11T03:14:57Z, no warnings \u2014 the check-in may come from another path (hotspot/cached) or be from before the outage, so it doesn't rule out a site outage. Not a single-laptop problem per KB-014 (several users affected), so KB-014 says escalate. Still needed: check office WAN/ISP circuit, edge firewall/router, core switch and DHCP/DNS for the affected site/floor; confirm which office/floor and when it started; contact the ISP if the circuit is down. Tier 1 tools can't see or fix network infrastructure.",
  "reason": "P1 office-wide network outage; KB-014 escalation criteria met; beyond Tier 1 tools"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for reporting this so fast. Since the whole floor is down, we've marked this as top priority and sent it straight to our Tier 2 network engineers. They'll check the office internet line, the firewall/router and the network equipment, and contact the internet provider if needed. It would help them a lot if you reply with your office location and floor, roughly when the outage started, and whether wired and Wi-Fi connections are both down. In the meantime, anyone who has to stay online can use a phone hotspot. We'll keep you posted as soon as we know more.",
  "internal_note": "P1 office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3). Account is active with no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online with last check-in 2026-10-11T03:14:57Z and no warnings. That check-in may have come from a hotspot or from before the outage, so it doesn't rule out a site outage. Several users are affected, so KB-014's escalation criteria apply. Tier 1 tools can't reach network infrastructure. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) to check the WAN/ISP circuit, edge firewall, core switching and DHCP/DNS. Asked the user for office location and floor, start time, and whether wired and Wi-Fi are both down.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
